On 21 Jul 2010, at 22:38, CosmicRay wrote:

> On 21 Jul 2010, at 22:34, Jonathan Jones wrote:
>=20
>> What is the benefit of lojgugde, the destination of the lead character, =
who is a visiting Terran, being secret from Terrans?=20
>=20
> Firstly, it'd make a great backstory if the story is contemporary, and wh=
y we - ordinary Terrans - haven't heard of it in our everyday matters.  Sec=
ondly, maybe you'll just have to watch and find out ;-)

Maybe that's not the most satisfying answer, I apologise.

Lindar's vision as I understand it is to create a near-perfect society for =
Lojgugde, approaching a utopia.

Without wishing to tip my hand too early on the scripting ideas, dropping i=
n a character who lives in a futuristic society already will not give the s=
ame sense of awe and wonder as someone who shares only our current mundane =
experience.

Viewers will relate better to someone who's undergoing the same discovery a=
s they are - I want our young viewers to feel privileged and excited to be =
sharing the revelations Alpha enjoys, rather than be made to feel like they=
're watching something that has no common root with their everyday world.

There are plenty of plot devices to do this, and they don't prevent Lojgugd=
e from being in its idealised state right now, with better technology and s=
o on.

kozmikreis

